  "question": {
    "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math> is a triangle in a plane with vertices <math><mi>A</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>B</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math><mi>C</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#956;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> . If the median through <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;is equally inclined to the coordinate axes, then the value of <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi>&#956;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> is",
    "image": null
